{"id": "q0013", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 728552883, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "c1188d4ab398808355719c420f025bd920b27aba798f5596eb328457a751cc63", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 4, "query": "Eve had 20 pieces of pomelos. After giving her friend some pomelos, Eve is left with 1/4 of the pomelos she originally had. How many pomelos did Eve give away?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0013.wav", "input_sha256": "985cf51b63efa06ff45836529161750579a6f6e7d110500e24fe9a1f665a7bed", "input_samples": 224200, "input_s": 14.012, "n_real_chunks": 15, "score": 0.1428, "act": 0.9989, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Eve had 20 pieces of pomelos to start with. After giving some away, she was left with a quarter of what she originally had. So, a quarter of 2 0 is 5. That means she gave away the rest. To find out how many she gave away, we subtract the 5 she has left from the original 2 0. Twenty minus five equals fifteen. So, E ve gave away fifteen pomelos.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 10, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 19, "feed_lag_max_ms": 892, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 3867, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0013_aggressive_local.wav", "sha256": "958bddfae88c602ca94c2a26523b7791b1750d15083b43c5ad27ab73025e8260", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 19.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.081, 1.147, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.086, 2.152, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.081, 3.147, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.077, 4.14, 1, 