{"id": "q0069", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2230889066, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "c1188d4ab398808355719c420f025bd920b27aba798f5596eb328457a751cc63", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 4, "query": "Every day Charisma meditates for 15 minutes when she first wakes up and again before she goes to sleep.  5 days a week she practices 1 hour of yoga.  in 4 weeks, how much time has she spent on meditation/yoga practice?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0069.wav", "input_sha256": "2ff180e10298b8c8113ff7403578312d58d33ac418339ccb4e0837230683d338", "input_samples": 279600, "input_s": 17.475, "n_real_chunks": 18, "score": 0.2302, "act": 0.9989, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "So every day she does 15 minutes of meditation twice, so that's 30 minutes a day. Plus one hour of yoga five days a week. So let's calculate the total time spent on these practices in four weeks. First, for meditation: 30 minutes per day times seven days is 2 10 minutes per week. Over four weeks, that' s 2 1 0 times four equals 8 40 minutes for meditation. Now for yoga: one hour is 6 0 minutes, and she does this five days a week, so that's 3 00 minutes per week. In four weeks, that would be 3 00 times four equal s 1, 200 minutes. Adding both together, 8 4 0 plus 1, 2 0 0 gives us 2,0 4 0 minutes. So in four weeks, Char isma has spent 2,04 0 minutes on her meditation and yoga practice s.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 17, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 