{"id": "q0101", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3720081385, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "c1188d4ab398808355719c420f025bd920b27aba798f5596eb328457a751cc63", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 4, "query": "Riproarin' Ringo was roping a recalcitrant dogie. Ringo decided to give the dogie a reprieve by calculating \\[|(1-i)^8|\\]before riding after the dogie. What answer should Ringo have found?\n\nSolve and give the final answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0101.wav", "input_sha256": "1ec9e7f5f9ada392c830d2d5b2f748a327a5dac43cbc6c5604f062faa0a5104d", "input_samples": 222000, "input_s": 13.875, "n_real_chunks": 14, "score": 0.4008, "act": 0.9976, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "1 i 8 means one times i to the eighth power. I is the square root of negative one, so let's see what happens when we raise it to different powers. If we start with i and multiply by itself, we get negative one. Then if we take that negative one and multi ply by i again, we get positive one. And then if we do it once more, we get back to i. So this pattern repeat s every four power s. That means i to the fourth power is one. Since eight is a multiple of four, i to the eighth power is just one times one, which is one. So Ringo should have found one.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 14, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 37, "feed_lag_max_ms": 5, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 5, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0101_aggressive_local.wav", "sha256": "7edd4c380bbdb67f620a873c6f1d44abd