{"id": "q0459", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2833011061, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "c1188d4ab398808355719c420f025bd920b27aba798f5596eb328457a751cc63", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 4, "query": "What are some basic spirits you should have at your bar", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0459.wav", "input_sha256": "b29397119c0a30b55bf41a0cf43e057efabfde6654c1c5de5231e6048ba54b24", "input_samples": 52400, "input_s": 3.275, "n_real_chunks": 4, "score": 0.7109, "act": 0.9989, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Some basic spirits to keep in a home bar are: Vodka — neutral base for martinis, Moscow mules, Bloody Marys , Gin — essential for gin & tonics, martinis, negronis , Rum — ideally white rum and/or dark rum for mojitos, daiquiris, rum & Coke , Tequila — preferably blanco or reposado for margaritas and palomas , Whiskey — bourbon or rye for Old Fashioneds, Manhattans, whiskey sours , Scotch — optional but good for sipping or classic cocktails , Brandy/Cognac — useful for sidecars, brandy Alexanders, or after-dinner drinks If you want a simple starter setup: vodka, gin, rum, tequila, bourbon/rye, and brandy will cover most classic cocktails.", "expert_answer": "Some basic spirits to keep in a home bar are:\n\n- **Vodka** — neutral base for martinis, Moscow mules, Bloody Marys\n- **Gin** — essential for gin & tonics, martinis, negronis\n- **Rum** — ideally **white rum** and/or **dark rum** for mojitos, daiquiris, rum & Coke\n- **Tequila** — preferably **blanco** or **reposado** for margaritas and palomas\n- **Whiskey** — bourbon or rye for Old Fashioneds, Manhattans, whiskey sours\n- **Scotch** — optional but good for sipping or classic cocktails\n- **Brandy/Cognac** — useful for sidecars, brandy Alexanders, or after-dinner drinks\n\nIf you want a simple starter setup: **vodka, gin, rum, tequila, bourbon/rye, and brandy** will cover most classic cocktails.", "transcript": "What are some basic spirits you should have at your bar?\n", "asr_s": 0.77, "expert_s": 4.66, "expert_input_samples": 52400, "expert_input_s": 3.275, "expert_input_sha256": "b29397119c0a30b55bf41a0cf43e057efabfde6654c1c5de5231e6048ba54b24", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 0.0, "relay_synth_ms": 32027, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 16, "feed_lag_max_ms": 159, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 159, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0459_aggressive_relay.wav", "sha256": "db9286f01e9c48e9b314df205b8eeb410beada7e58c39ad8733b80f126e9c77c", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 50.76}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0459_aggressive_stall.wav", "sha256": "100ff08b0d75504f22473657feecb609b654260128d614f80dcb8f71fcc38fca", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 17.2}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.08, 1.144, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.081, 2.145, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.086, 3.152, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 3.275, 3.353, 3.72, 0, 0, 0], [4, 0, 4.275, 4.522, 5.183, 0, 24000, 0], [5, 0, 5.275, 5.356, 6.108, 0, 24000, 0], [6, 0, 6.275, 6.358, 7.185, 0, 24000, 0], [7, 0, 7.275, 7.358, 8.183, 0, 24000, 0], [8, 0, 8.275, 8.359, 9.161, 0, 24000, 0], [9, 0, 9.275, 9.362, 10.165, 0, 24000, 0], [10, 0, 10.275, 10.357, 11.175, 0, 24000, 0], [11, 0, 11.275, 11.359, 12.213, 0, 24000, 0], [12, 0, 12.275, 12.356, 13.103, 0, 24000, 0], [13, 0, 13.275, 13.357, 14.164, 0, 24000, 0], [14, 0, 14.275, 14.355, 15.18, 0, 24000, 0], [15, 0, 15.275, 15.358, 16.061, 0, 24000, 0], [16, 0, 16.275, 16.354, 17.176, 0, 24000, 0], [17, 0, 17.275, 17.356, 18.258, 0, 24000, 0], [18, 0, 18.275, 18.359, 19.139, 0, 24000, 0], [19, 0, 19.275, 19.359, 20.006, 0, 28800, 1]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 3.275, "last_real_feed_done": 3.353, "onset": 3.72, "gate_read_done": 3.72, "fire": 3.72, "candidate_first_pcm": null, "stall_note": 3.721, "stall_first_pcm": 4.434, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 20.006, "expert_req": 3.721, "expert_resp": 9.152, "relay_synth_start": 20.006, "relay_first_pcm": 20.899, "relay_synth_end": 52.033, "first_any_pcm": 4.434, "first_answer_pcm": 20.899, "session_end": 52.489}, "ttfa_answer_s": 17.624, "ttfa_any_s": 1.159}
{"id": "q0471", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2486287301, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "c1188d4ab398808355719c420f025bd920b27aba798f5596eb328457a751cc63", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 4, "query": "Write a brief summary of Nezami Ganjavi's Layli and Majnun.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0471.wav", "input_sha256": "753fa957c5512aac4f6e62036c5d62394ed88c266b3e9dfc3fab80d8f1a6c79c", "input_samples": 55800, "input_s": 3.487, "n_real_chunks": 4, "score": 0.6716, "act": 0.9997, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Nizami Ganjavi’s Layli and Majnun is a 12th-century Persian narrative poem about the tragic love of Qays and Layli. Qays falls deeply in love with Layli, but their relationship is forbidden by social and family pressures. His obsessive devotion earns him the name Majnun, meaning “madman,” and he withdraws into the wilderness, composing poetry and living among animals. Ultimately, both lovers die without being united in life, and the poem becomes a powerful meditation on love, longing, spiritual devotion, and the conflict between personal passion and social convention.", "expert_answer": "**Nizami Ganjavi’s *Layli and Majnun*** is a 12th-century Persian narrative poem about the tragic love of Qays and Layli. Qays falls deeply in love with Layli, but their relationship is forbidden by social and family pressures. His obsessive devotion earns him the name **Majnun**, meaning “madman,” and he withdraws into the wilderness, composing poetry and living among animals. Layli is forced to marry another man, though she remains emotionally faithful to Majnun. Ultimately, both lovers die without being united in life, and the poem becomes a powerful meditation on love, longing, spiritu